WEBVTT

NOTE Teaching tape 1997 v6 "Understanding Your Roots": every spoken line (the picture and its bar carry the words; offer these OFF by default).

1
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:06.911
TriedPath Fellowship presents:

2
00:00:07.296 --> 00:00:08.818
Understanding Your Roots.

3
00:00:09.918 --> 00:00:11.726
Part one. How your mind works.

4
00:00:12.088 --> 00:00:14.311
Our mind works like a computer.

5
00:00:14.557 --> 00:00:18.144
It is constantly placing information into
categories.

6
00:00:18.544 --> 00:00:21.519
If you feed something destructive into
your mind,

7
00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.745
it will add this to a stack

8
00:00:23.745 --> 00:00:26.107
of similar material already there.

9
00:00:26.507 --> 00:00:29.516
As the stack grows larger, it gains in
power.

10
00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:32.541
In the computer industry, the saying is:

11
00:00:32.857 --> 00:00:34.732
garbage in, garbage out.

12
00:00:37.532 --> 00:00:38.511
Question two.

13
00:00:38.909 --> 00:00:43.557
Have you ever been able to stop thinking
about something? Did you succeed?

14
00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:45.967
New from TriedPath:

15
00:00:46.338 --> 00:00:47.466
Mountains of Material!

16
00:00:47.766 --> 00:00:50.762
Fill your memory tapes, and push the old
material out!

17
00:00:51.062 --> 00:00:52.554
Operators are standing by!

18
00:00:53.854 --> 00:00:54.541
Part two.

19
00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:55.694
Displacement.

20
00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.272
Putting off, putting on.

21
00:00:57.672 --> 00:01:01.674
Displacement is the idea that one thing
pushes out another.

22
00:01:01.803 --> 00:01:03.508
There is no neutral ground.

23
00:01:03.908 --> 00:01:06.856
If there is a vacancy there, evil will
fill it.

24
00:01:07.806 --> 00:01:10.102
Turn on any radio or television,

25
00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:13.130
and you will find a mind-boggling barrage

26
00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:14.971
of new morality propaganda.

27
00:01:15.371 --> 00:01:18.694
Gays on television are shown as superior
people.

28
00:01:21.594 --> 00:01:22.674
Question five.

29
00:01:23.076 --> 00:01:26.804
What do you do when associations from the
past overwhelm you?

30
00:01:28.323 --> 00:01:30.011
The TriedPath Pocket Library.

31
00:01:30.311 --> 00:01:32.945
The roots, the way out, and help for the
family.

32
00:01:33.245 --> 00:01:34.495
Just one dollar each.

33
00:01:37.045 --> 00:01:40.989
Homosexual people say they never asked for
their orientation.

34
00:01:41.364 --> 00:01:43.631
In most cases, that is true.

35
00:01:44.181 --> 00:01:45.739
Something they never chose.
